From 369378dc1552ae46f7f95a598a085c0025e464b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hugo Sales <hugo@hsal.es>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:52:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: Open the PCI sysfs config file through init's root on
 Linux 7.3

Linux 7.3 starts every kthread in an empty nullfs (commit 32750c77e811d,
"fs: start all kthreads in nullfs"), so path lookups from kthreads fail.
nv_get_pci_sysfs_config() runs in one during module init: the PCI async
probe worker in the open build, and the nv-probe-<bdf> kthread in both.
Its filp_open() of /sys/bus/pci/devices/<bdf>/config then fails,
sysfs_config_file stays NULL, nv_dynamic_power_available() returns false
and RM reports "Runtime D3 status: Not supported". The GPU never runtime
suspends

The packaged source patch opens the file inside scoped_with_init_fs()
where userspace_init_fs is available to the module. That covers the open
build. A non-GPL build can't use it, since userspace_init_fs is
EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL, but it has no async probe either, so the kthread only
serializes the same work. Probe inline there when
NV_PCI_ASYNC_PROBE_SUPPORTED is 0

A probe after module init (sysfs bind, hotplug) already ran inline and is
not affected
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-pci.c
@@ -1682,8 +1682,15 @@ nv_pci_probe
      * run concurrently via the async worker pool. Later bind/unbind from
      * sysfs or hotplug is synchronous, so the kthread overhead is not
      * worthwhile.
+     *
+     * Without async probe, probes are serialized and the kthread adds no
+     * parallelism. It would also lose the caller's root on Linux 7.3+,
+     * where kthreads start in nullfs and nv_get_pci_sysfs_config() can't
+     * open the config file without scoped_with_init_fs(), which needs the
+     * GPL-only userspace_init_fs.
      */
-    if (!smp_load_acquire(&nv_pci_driver_registration_in_progress))
+    if (!NV_PCI_ASYNC_PROBE_SUPPORTED ||
+        !smp_load_acquire(&nv_pci_driver_registration_in_progress))
     {
         return nv_pci_probe_body(pci_dev, id_table);
     }
